{
  "_readme": [
    "Every conversation in the game. Edit the text, save, and play the scene again: this file is re-read at each level start (in the browser no rebuild is needed; on the phone, use the tuning panel > scenes to edit lines live).",
    "A scene is a list of beats. Each beat can have: shot, do, who + say, card, wait.",
    "  who / say : speaker id and the line. Tap advances. Speaker ids: 'player', a cast id, or 'boss' / 'them' for the enemy that triggered the scene.",
    "  shot      : 'kind:actor' - kinds: front, close, low, hands, over, wide, crowd, side (side also takes 'with': other actor).",
    "  do        : { actor: action or [actions] }, '*' = every cast member.",
    "              enemy actions : point, laugh, beckon, chicken, cower, stomp, yawn, idle, enter (step off the sidewalk), come (walk up to the player), flee, ko",
    "              player actions: bare (plain hands), gloves (puts the slapping hands on), phone, look, shrug, point, vow, idle, slap:<actor>",
    "  card      : big title text.   wait: seconds before a beat with no line moves on.",
    "cast (optional): enemies placed for the scene only - x in metres across the street, z in metres ahead of the player, sidewalk: true to start them on the kerb.",
    "When scenes play: 'intro' before the first level; 'intro_<levelId>' before any level; 'boss_<type>' when a boss wakes up; 'outro_<levelId>' after it falls;",
    "a level spawn with \"scene\": \"name\" plays that scene when the enemy gets close (it is 'them').",
    "play: 'always' | 'once' (per device) | 'never'."
  ],
